{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0431","billNumberShort":"H.B. 431","billNumberLong":"HB0431S01","fileNumber":"2026FL1417","shortTitle":"Wildlife Crossing Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"CHEWSH","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Chew, Scott H.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"OWENSD","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Owens, Derrin R.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill creates an account and provides funding for wildlife connectivity and livestock protection projects.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>creates the Wildlife Crossing Account in the Transportation Investment Fund of 2005 for projects that improve wildlife safety and connectivity and livestock safety;<hr><ltbullet>creates an earmark for sales and use tax revenue to be deposited into the account;<hr><ltbullet>defines allowed uses of money in the account;<hr><ltbullet>directs the Department of Transportation, in consultation with the Division of Wildlife Resources and stakeholders, to recommend projects to the Transportation Commission for prioritization;<hr><ltbullet>creates the option for applicants for a vehicle registration or hunting and other licenses to make a voluntary contribution to support wildlife connectivity; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Kurt P. Gasser","fiscalAnalyst":"Andrea Wilko","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/18/2026","trackingID":"RQOABABLMR","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 09:17:26.313","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-